ergon-io info: connect_background's dial helper and the warning thread go on CPU 0: Config::helper_cpus. This process may use CPUs 0-7 (its cgroup cpuset, /sys/fs/cgroup/cpuset.cpus.effective); the polling CPU is 2.
ergon-io warning: N2 warn: enP44106s2: interrupts are deferred (napi_defer_hard_irqs 2, gro_flush_timeout 200000 ns) but no socket on it busy-polls: packets wait for the 200 µs timer. Fix: `echo 0 > /sys/class/net/enP44106s2/napi_defer_hard_irqs; echo 0 > /sys/class/net/enP44106s2/gro_flush_timeout`, or turn busy polling on (evidence: Linux Documentation/networking/napi.rst; the lab sets them only with busy polling (md-dpdk/benches/cloud/vm.sh); not measured here) (ERGON_HOST_CHECKS=off silences host-check warnings)
ergon-io warning: T19 warn: the loop thread (/proc/thread-self/stat) took 1085 minor and 0 major page faults since the last check (minflt 23 → 1108, majflt 0 → 0): each stops the thread while the kernel maps the page in, and a major one waits for I/O too (not measured here). Fix: touch and lock its memory before the loop (`mlockall(MCL_CURRENT | MCL_FUTURE)`, every buffer written once), and keep the kernel from moving its pages: T3 (THP), T5 (NUMA balancing), T14 (compaction), T17 (KSM) (evidence: Linux proc(5) (/proc/<pid>/task/<tid>/stat: minflt, field 10; majflt, field 12); not measured here) (ERGON_HOST_CHECKS=off silences host-check warnings)
